    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`mapper/Timezone.java`** (new) \u2014 helper mirroring the existing `Locality`/`ContactPreference` pattern. Maps a region to its IANA name (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`), returning `null` for absent/unknown regions.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `timezone` using expression `Timezone.of(Locality.of(owner.getCustomerCode()))`, so the timezone is derived from the same region (`locality`) already computed from the customer code.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema (placed after `locality`), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new getter/setter at build time.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class) passes: a Sydney owner (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) returns `locality: \"NSW\"` and `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"`. Full `mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
